    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72222.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "Well, your guess is as good as mine. I mean, the problem is that our so-called majority in the Senate is a 50-50 majority. It's only a majority because we can call in Vice President Harris to break the tie if we have all 50 Democratic senators together. But if one defects like, you know, Senator Manchin or Senator Sinema, they decide to take a walk on us, then we no longer have the ability to create the 50-50 tie to be broken. So we've got FDR-style ambitions to bring progressive change and equality in freedom and justice to everybody in America, but we just don't have FDR-style majorities. When Roosevelt was in power, he had dozens of more representatives and 25 or 30 more senators than the Republicans did, and we're trying to deal with the crises of our time with these extremely slender majorities.",
