  {
    "episode_id": 72222,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72222.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "Well, yeah, sure, he's got a point. And I hear this wherever I go that, you know, we don't have a problem with our politics or the policies we've been advancing. We got a problem with the messaging. And so let's consider the contest on. I mean, I'm out there telling all the young people, here's my message. Everything that you need to know about voting is everything you need to know about driving. If you want to go forward, you put it in D, if you want to go backwards, you put it in R. How's that for a message? And everything flows out of that. If we want to make progress, you got to be on the side of democracy, which is the Democratic Party, because forgive my partisanship here, but I am an elected partisan figure, and I would just say if you know, whatever our flaws, whatever our imperfections and messaging or anything else, we are the party of democracy and we are standing up to defend the Constitution and our democratic arrangements in the country. And we're not going to get anything done if we go down the road of the Oath Keepers and the three percenters in Marjorie Taylor Greene. and Lauren Bobert and Matt Gaetz and so on. We're not. I mean, that is a party that's been taken over for nihilism and the destruction of democratic purposes.",
