  {
    "episode_id": 72222,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72222.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "You know, what we're going to have is a clash between two kinds of populism and one is going to be right wing authoritarian populism, which picks out scapegoats like, you know, Mexican rapists or critical race theory or LGBTQ groomers. Or we're going to have a progressive populism that is focused on the real life situation of diabetics and people who need prescription drugs. And we are going to focus on the stranglehold that big money has over Washington and over a lot of politicians. So I view all of those issues of the week that they come up with. you know critical race theory or groomers or what have you as just attempts to distract people it's an attempt to bedazzle people but it's it's meaningless and but it is more dangerous than that because they're often trying to inflame racial ethnic religious feelings and that is the playbook of right-wing populism all over the earth right now",
