    "turn_idx": 39,
    "turn_text": "Well, let's talk about the Earth for just a little bit. I know we have to let you go soon, but we're seeing a war in Europe and a war that has been fueled by exactly the kind of demagoguery and populism that you mentioned on the Russian side, specifically. In the wake of the need, in the face of the need, we're seeing massive military, you know, dedications, procurements and and contracts. We're seeing a lot of money being spent on military provisions for the Ukrainians. $33 billion in the last few days. It's approaching $50 billion in the last two months. Most of that going directly to military operations. And then at home, we still have this so-called defense budget that's eating up $0.53 of every dollar. We just came, and last time I spoke to you, I had just come from doing a story about how a lot of that military contract of money trickles down to privatized military facilities and training places that we were able to show were places where people that came to the capital had trained. Are we ever going to see any attention to this or does the urgent need in Ukraine sort of, as you to use your word, bedazzle us from a bigger agenda of shrinking our military spending?",
