    "turn_text": "Well, I want to come back to your experience in the last few months, but before I do, just quickly, we're constantly told to write to our congressperson. And we're also told to be out in the streets demonstrating, if we don't like what's happening. Do either of those things actually make a difference? Do you see anyone paying attention to demonstrations outside? I've been in lots of them, so I'm all for it, but I've always wondered, do people inside actually even hear the screams and yells?",
